From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:02:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [GDN] int16 row-scaled recurrent state
 (--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype int16)

Stores the GatedDeltaNet state as int16 codes plus one fp32 scale per
(head, v) row, packed per head as [V + 2, K] int16 so whole-block copies
(prefix-cache align mode, spec decode) stay format-agnostic. Kernels load
code*scale into fp32 and re-quantize on every store (amax/32767, rint).

- packed non-spec decode and fused sigmoid-gating (spec/mixed) decode:
  STATE_INT16 constexpr path
- prefill: Triton chunk backend forced; int16 dequant gather / quant
  scatter kernels around it
- MTP CUDA kernel falls back to the Triton spec path (unsupported dtype)
- warmup, state shape/dtype plumbing, unit tests

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Release note: rebased onto the recover-spec patches (01-*). The two conflict
hunks (imports in qwen_gdn_linear_attn.py; MambaStateDtypeCalculator in
mamba_utils.py) are resolved exactly as in the measured build's merge commit.
